window.RENDRIX_DOCS = {
  "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md": "# Architecture\n\nRendrix is a rendering engine and application runtime. TypeScript applications run inside it and are\ndrawn by its own GPU pipeline: there is no Chromium, Electron, WebView or system browser involved,\nand Rendrix makes no attempt to be API-compatible with any of them.\n\n```\n your TypeScript / TSX            rendrix CLI (Node)                       rendrix-runtime (Rust)\n ───────────────────  build ───▶  type-check, transpile to ES modules ──▶  ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n index.html, styles.css           pack  .rdxapp  (JSON bundle)             │ rendrix-js   QuickJS + Web APIs│\n                                  or  standalone executable                │ rendrix-core DOM → style →     │\n                                                                           │              boxes → layout →  │\n        OS input ◀──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │              display list      │\n        (winit)  ──▶ Session ──▶ DOM events ──▶ your handlers ──▶ DOM ───▶ │ rendrix-gfx  wgpu renderer    │\n                                                                           └──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Crates (`engine/crates/`)\n\n| Crate | Responsibility | Interface other crates rely on |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rendrix-css` | Tokenizer/parser, selectors + specificity, cascade, inheritance, custom properties (`var()`), media queries, `@keyframes`, timing functions, interpolation, computed style | `SelectorElement` trait (style any tree), `ComputedStyle`, `compute_style` |\n| `rendrix-dom` | Arena DOM: nodes, attributes, mutation records, selector queries, tolerant HTML parser/serializer, form state, dirty tracking, node GC | `Document`; `ElRef` implements `SelectorElement` |\n| `rendrix-layout` | Layout-engine-neutral box tree and the `LayoutEngine` trait; a persistent Taffy backend (flex, grid, block) that only re-lays out what changed | `LayoutNode`, `LayoutEngine`, `TextMeasurer` |\n| `rendrix-gfx` | Display list, cosmic-text shaping + paragraph cache, glyph atlas, wgpu renderer (SDF rounded rects/borders/gradients/shadows/clips/transforms, images, text) | `DisplayList`, `TextSystem`, `Renderer` |\n| `rendrix-core` | `Engine`: DOM → styles (+transitions/animations) → box generation (block/inline/flex/grid, anonymous boxes, whitespace, replaced elements, form controls) → layout → painting; hit testing, scrolling, text editing | `Engine::update(now)`, `hit_test`, `edit`, `display_list` |\n| `rendrix-js` | `JsEngine` trait + QuickJS backend, ES module loader, DOM and Web API prelude (JavaScript), host operations, event-loop glue | `JsEngine`, `Host`, `JsRuntime` |\n| `rendrix-runtime` | App bundle loader, `Session` (input state machine and frame loop), winit window driver, headless driver, benchmark | `Session`, `AppBundle` |\n\n## One frame\n\n1. **Platform events** (winit) are translated by the window driver into `Session` calls: `pointer_move`,\n   `pointer_down`, `key_down`, `wheel`, `text_commit`, `resize`.\n2. `Session` hit-tests against the previous frame's geometry and dispatches **real DOM events**\n   (`pointerover/enter/move/down/up`, `mouse*`, `click`, `keydown`, `input`, `change`, `focus*`, `wheel`…)\n   through the JavaScript event system with capture → target → bubble phases. Default actions run only if\n   no handler called `preventDefault()`: focus, click activation (checkbox, radio, label, form submit),\n   caret placement and drag-selection, Tab traversal, text editing, scrolling.\n3. Timers, completed fetches and microtasks run; then `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks.\n4. `Engine::update(now)`:\n   - rebuild stylesheets if `<style>`/`<link>` or the media context changed;\n   - **restyle** only what changed: dirty subtrees for attribute/class/inline-style changes; for\n     hover/active/focus and child-list changes only the element itself, descending when the computed style\n     changed or the stylesheet has non-local state/structural selectors;\n   - if no computed style actually changed (most hovers), the frame stops here;\n   - start transitions/keyframe animations from style changes and sample running ones;\n   - build the box tree (formatting-context rules, anonymous boxes) and run layout (Taffy keeps its tree\n     between frames, so unchanged subtrees reuse cached results);\n   - paint to a **display list** with stacking order, clips, transforms and viewport culling, producing\n     the hit-test list in the same traversal.\n5. `Renderer` flattens the display list into one instance buffer and draws it in a single pipeline and\n   usually one draw call.\n\nAn idle application does no work: no timer, no animation and no pending change means no frame.\n\n## Replaceable parts\n\n* **JavaScript engine.** Only `quickjs.rs` names `rquickjs`. The rest of the runtime talks to a `JsEngine`\n  trait (eval script/module, call a global, drain jobs) and exposes native functionality through a single\n  entry point, `__native(op, ...args)`, implemented by `Host`. The Web API surface is JavaScript\n  (`prelude/*.js`) built on those operations, so another engine needs the trait implementation and the same\n  entry point.\n* **Layout engine.** Layout consumes `LayoutNode` + `ComputedStyle`, never DOM types. Taffy is one\n  implementation of `LayoutEngine`.\n* **Text.** Layout measures through `TextMeasurer`; only `rendrix-gfx` shapes text.\n\n## Modules and TypeScript\n\nThe runtime never sees TypeScript. `rendrix build` type-checks with the project's `tsconfig.json`, transpiles\nevery module to ES2022 with the TypeScript compiler API, resolves bare specifiers from `node_modules`\n(ESM only), rewrites imports to bundle paths and emits a `rendrix-app/1` JSON bundle. QuickJS loads the\nmodules natively (static imports, `import()`, top-level `await`). JSX compiles to\n`rendrix/jsx-runtime`, which builds DOM nodes directly (no virtual DOM).\n\n## Memory model\n\nDOM nodes live in a Rust arena. JavaScript wrappers are weak handles registered with a\n`FinalizationRegistry`; wrappers of connected nodes are also held strongly so identity, expando properties\nand listeners survive GC. Listener state is keyed by node id, never stored on the wrapper. Detached subtrees\nwith no live wrapper are freed by a periodic sweep and their ids reused.\n\n## Known architectural limits\n\n* The box tree is rebuilt in full after any style or structure change (≈5 ms per 9,000 nodes); only layout\n  results are incremental. Incremental box generation is the next performance step.\n* Overlay scrollbars are painted but not interactive; there is no accessibility tree yet\n  ([ACCESSIBILITY_PLAN.md](ACCESSIBILITY_PLAN.md)).\n* Absolutely positioned boxes use the containing block's origin when their insets are `auto` (no static\n  position), and inline elements with box styling (padding, background…) behave as inline-blocks.\n* A single window and a single JavaScript context per process.\n\nSee [COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md) for exactly what is and is not supported, and\n[ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md](ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md) for the roadmap.\n",
  "docs/COMPATIBILITY.md": "# Compatibility matrix\r\n\r\nRendrix is **not a browser** and does not claim browser compatibility. This page lists what is\r\nimplemented and covered by an automated test (✅), implemented with known gaps (🟡), and not\r\nimplemented (❌). Anything not listed is not supported. Tests live next to the code:\r\n`engine/crates/*/src` (unit), `engine/crates/rendrix-runtime/tests` (input/frame integration, GPU pixels),\r\n`packages/cli/test` (build pipeline, runs bundles in the real runtime).\r\n\r\nVerified platform: **Windows 11, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060, Vulkan** (windowed at 125 % DPI and headless).\r\nmacOS and Linux share the same code (winit, wgpu, arboard) but have **not been built or run**.\r\n\r\n## JavaScript and modules\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| ES2023 language, classes, private fields, `async`/`await`, generators | ✅ | Whatever QuickJS-ng provides; `BigInt`, `WeakRef`, `FinalizationRegistry`, `Object.groupBy`, `toSorted`, `Array.fromAsync` are present |\r\n| ES modules, relative imports, top-level `await` | ✅ | Bare specifiers resolved at build time (ESM packages only) |\r\n| Dynamic `import()` | 🟡 | Provided by QuickJS; the build rewrites specifiers, not covered by a test |\r\n| CommonJS / `require` / Node built-ins | ❌ | Build error with an explanation |\r\n| TypeScript, TSX | ✅ | Type-checked + transpiled at build time; the runtime executes JavaScript only |\r\n| Promises, microtask order, `queueMicrotask`, unhandled-rejection events | ✅ | |\r\n| `setTimeout`/`setInterval`/`requestAnimationFrame` | ✅ | Frame-driven rAF; timers on the platform clock |\r\n| `Intl`, `WebAssembly`, Workers, `Temporal` | ❌ | Not defined (checked in the runtime); `toLocaleString` works without locale data |\r\n\r\n## DOM\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Node, Element, Text, Comment, Document, DocumentFragment, tree mutation, errors as `DOMException` | ✅ | |\r\n| Attributes, `classList`, `dataset`, `style` (live), `innerHTML`/`outerHTML`, `insertAdjacent*`, `cloneNode` | ✅ | HTML parser is tolerant, not the full HTML5 tree builder (no foster parenting) |\r\n| `querySelector(All)`, `matches`, `closest`, `getElementsBy*` | ✅ | Type/class/id/attribute selectors, all combinators, `:not :is :where :nth-* :first/last-child :empty :root :hover :active :focus :disabled :checked`. `:has()` ❌ |\r\n| Events: capture/target/bubble, `once`, `passive`, `signal`, `on*` properties, `stopImmediatePropagation`, `CustomEvent` | ✅ | |\r\n| Mouse/Pointer/Wheel/Keyboard/Input/Focus/Submit events from the OS | ✅ | Touch and gamepad input are ❌; pointer capture is a no-op |\r\n| Form controls: `input` (text-like, checkbox, radio, button), `textarea`, `select`, `button`, `label`, `form` | 🟡 | Typing, caret, selection, clipboard, `input`/`change`, label and submit activation work. No undo, no validation UI, `select` has no popup list, file/date/range inputs ❌ |\r\n| `getBoundingClientRect`, `offset*`, `client*`, `scroll*`, `scrollIntoView`, `elementFromPoint`, `getComputedStyle` | 🟡 | `getComputedStyle` implements a fixed list of properties (display, position, colour, size, margin/padding/border, font, opacity, overflow, z-index, transform, custom properties); others return `\"\"` |\r\n| `MutationObserver` | ✅ | childList, attributes (+filter, old value), characterData, subtree |\r\n| `ResizeObserver` | 🟡 | One content-box size; delivered per frame |\r\n| `IntersectionObserver`, Shadow DOM, custom elements, `Range`/`Selection`, `contenteditable`, drag and drop | ❌ | APIs are absent or throw `NotSupportedError` so feature detection works |\r\n\r\n## CSS\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Cascade: origin, specificity, `!important`, source order, inheritance, `inherit`/`initial`/`unset`, custom properties and `var()` with fallbacks | ✅ | |\r\n| Media queries (`width`, `height`, `orientation`, `prefers-color-scheme`, `resolution`, `and`/`not`/`,`) | ✅ | Re-evaluated on resize |\r\n| Box model, `box-sizing`, margin/padding/border, `border-radius` | ✅ | Per-side border colour and dashed/dotted styles render as one solid colour |\r\n| `display`: block, inline, inline-block, flex, inline-flex, grid, none, contents | ✅ | `table*` and `list-item` are not implemented (lists get a marker run) |\r\n| Flexbox (all properties) | ✅ | Taffy |\r\n| Grid (tracks, `repeat`, `minmax`, `fr`, auto-fill/fit, line and span placement, gaps) | ✅ | `grid-template-areas` ❌ |\r\n| Positioning: relative, absolute, fixed, z-index and stacking order | 🟡 | `sticky` behaves as relative; static position of auto-inset absolutes is the container origin |\r\n| Overflow: hidden/clip/scroll/auto, wheel scrolling, nested scrollers | ✅ | Scrollbars are overlay indicators, not draggable |\r\n| Floats, multi-column, tables, `writing-mode` | ❌ | |\r\n| Text: font family/size/weight/style, line-height, letter-spacing, alignment, decoration, transform, `white-space`, wrapping | ✅ | Shaping is cosmic-text (bidi/complex scripts are not covered by tests). `text-overflow: ellipsis` parsed, not drawn; `text-shadow`, `word-break`, `line-clamp` ❌ |\r\n| Colours (hex, `rgb`, `hsl`, named, alpha), gradients (linear/radial, ≤ 4 stops), `box-shadow` (outer + inset), `opacity`, `background-image: url()`, `object-fit` | 🟡 | Shadow blur is an analytic approximation; opacity applies per item, not as an offscreen group |\r\n| 2D `transform`, `transform-origin` | ✅ | No 3D, no `perspective` |\r\n| Transitions and `@keyframes` animations | ✅ | Animatable: opacity, colours, lengths, margin/padding, inset, transform, box-shadow, gap, flex-grow, font-size. Others switch discretely |\r\n| `calc()` | 🟡 | Only when all operands are the same kind (px-only or %-only) |\r\n| `@font-face` | 🟡 | Local bundled TTF/OTF/TTC only; WOFF/WOFF2 ❌ |\r\n| `::before`/`::after` with string `content` | ✅ | `attr()`, counters, images ❌ |\r\n| `filter`, `backdrop-filter`, `clip-path`, `mask`, `@container`, `@layer` ordering, nesting, `@import` | ❌ | `@supports`/`@layer` blocks are flattened |\r\n\r\n## Web platform APIs\r\n\r\n| API | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `URL`, `URLSearchParams` | ✅ | No IDNA/punycode |\r\n| `TextEncoder`, `TextDecoder` | ✅ | UTF-8, latin1/ascii |\r\n| `AbortController`/`AbortSignal` (`timeout`, `any`) | ✅ | |\r\n| `fetch`, `Headers`, `Request`, `Response`, `Blob` | 🟡 | Relative URLs read bundled assets; `data:` URLs; `http(s)` only when `permissions.network` is true. No streaming bodies, `FormData`, cookies, CORS or caching |\r\n| `localStorage`, `sessionStorage` | ✅ | Local storage is a per-user JSON file keyed by app name; no `storage` events |\r\n| `crypto.getRandomValues`, `randomUUID` | ✅ | OS CSPRNG; `crypto.subtle` ❌ |\r\n| `structuredClone`, `atob`/`btoa`, `performance.now`, `matchMedia`, `console` | ✅ | |\r\n| `navigator.clipboard` | 🟡 | Text only; fed by Copy/Cut in text controls |\r\n| Images via `<img>`, CSS backgrounds, `new Image()` with `load`/`error` | 🟡 | PNG is tested. JPEG, GIF (first frame) and WebP go through the same `image`-crate decoder but have no tests. No SVG, no animation |\r\n| `location`, `history` | 🟡 | In-memory; there is no navigation |\r\n| Canvas 2D, WebGL, WebGPU, `<video>`/`<audio>` | ❌ | `getContext()` returns `null` |\r\n| WebSocket, XMLHttpRequest, Web Workers, Service Workers, IndexedDB, Notifications, Geolocation | ❌ | Not defined |\r\n| `rendrix` module: `window`, `clipboard`, `quit`, `fs` | ✅ | `fs` is limited to directories listed in `permissions.fs_read`/`fs_write` |\r\n\r\n## Application platform\r\n\r\n| Capability | Status |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Native window (winit), DPI scaling, resize, title, close | ✅ Windows (verified); macOS/Linux ❓ untested |\r\n| Mouse, keyboard, wheel, text input, IME commit | ✅ Windows (IME composition itself untested) |\r\n| System clipboard | ✅ via `arboard` (text) |\r\n| Single standalone executable (`rendrix package`) | ✅ Windows (13.8 MB, no external runtime) |\r\n| File dialogs, multi-window, tray, global shortcuts, auto-update, accessibility tree | ❌ planned ([ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md](ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md)) |\r\n| Code signing / installers | ❌ (helper scripts from the previous tooling remain in `packages/cli/src`, unwired) |\r\n",
  "docs/BUILDING.md": "# Building and running\n\n## Requirements\n\n* Rust (stable) and a C/C++ toolchain: MSVC Build Tools on Windows, Xcode command line tools on macOS,\n  `build-essential` plus X11/Wayland development headers on Linux.\n* Node.js 18+ (the CLI and the TypeScript compiler). Bun or npm both work for installing.\n* A GPU with a Vulkan, Metal or DirectX 12 driver. The runtime picks the adapter itself;\n  `rendrix doctor` prints which one.\n\nOnly Windows has been exercised so far (see [COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md)).\n\n## Build the runtime\n\n```sh\ncd engine\ncargo test --workspace                      # ~160 Rust tests (GPU tests skip themselves with no adapter)\ncargo build --release -p rendrix-runtime    # engine/target/release/rendrix-runtime[.exe]\n```\n\nThe CLI finds the runtime through `RENDRIX_RUNTIME`, then `engine/target/{release,debug}`, then\n`$RENDRIX_HOME/runtime/<platform>-<arch>/`.\n\n## Create and run an application\n\n```sh\nnpm install                                  # once, at the repository root (installs TypeScript)\nnode packages/cli/bin/rendrix.mjs init my-app\ncd my-app\nrendrix dev        # builds, opens a native window, rebuilds and restarts on every change\nrendrix build      # type-check + compile to dist/my-app.rdxapp\nrendrix run        # build and run once\nrendrix check      # type-check only\nrendrix package    # dist/my-app.exe: one standalone executable, no Node/Bun/browser needed\nrendrix doctor     # Node, TypeScript, runtime, GPU adapter, project config\n```\n\nA project is `rendrix.json` (name, window size/title, permissions), an `index.html` (with `<link\nrel=\"stylesheet\">` and `<script type=\"module\" src=\"…ts|tsx\">`), `src/**`, and any assets. `tsconfig.json`\nselects `\"jsx\": \"react-jsx\"` and `\"jsxImportSource\": \"rendrix\"`.\n\n`rendrix dev` rebuilds and **restarts** the app on change; it does not preserve in-memory state. Hot state\npreservation is not implemented.\n\n## Verifying a build\n\n```sh\nnpm test                 # cargo test --workspace + the CLI test suite (runs bundles in the real runtime)\nnpm run e2e              # builds examples/app-counter, replays scripted clicks/resizes headlessly on the GPU,\n                         # fails if any expectation breaks, writes screenshots to .rendrix-shots/\nnpm run bench            # frame-pipeline timings on a 1,000-item list (release build)\n```\n\nRuntime flags useful for debugging: `--headless --screenshot out.png`, `--script steps.json`\n(steps: `click`, `move`, `type`, `key`, `wheel`, `resize`, `wait`, `settle`, `eval`, `expect`, `screenshot`),\n`--size WxH`, `--scale S`. Environment: `RENDRIX_DUMP_FRAME=file.png` writes the frame the window presents,\n`RENDRIX_TRACE_EVENTS=1` logs window events.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\n`engine/Cargo.lock` is committed; Rust dependencies resolve from it. The JavaScript side uses the\nTypeScript compiler version from `package.json`. Release profile: thin LTO, `opt-level = 3`.\n",
  "docs/SAFETY.md": "# Safety and permissions\n\n**Rendrix runs your application's code with the privileges of the user who starts it, plus a small set of\ncapability checks. It is not a sandbox for hostile code.** Only run applications you trust.\n\n## What is enforced\n\n| Capability | Default | How it is enforced |\n|---|---|---|\n| Network (`fetch` to `http(s)`) | **denied** | `permissions.network` in `rendrix.json`; otherwise `fetch` rejects with a `TypeError`. There is no per-host allow-list yet. |\n| File reads | **denied** | Only through `rendrix.fs`; paths are canonicalised and must lie inside a directory listed in `permissions.fs_read`. Plain Web APIs cannot touch the filesystem. |\n| File writes | **denied** | Same, with `permissions.fs_write`. |\n| Relative `fetch`, images, fonts, stylesheets | bundled assets only | `DirAssets` and bundle assets reject `..` segments. |\n| Process spawning, native add-ons, Node/Bun APIs | **do not exist** | There is no such API in the runtime. |\n| Remote script/module loading | **do not exist** | The build refuses `http(s):`/`node:` imports; the module loader only reads the bundle. |\n\nCovered by tests: `filesystem_access_is_permission_gated` (reads, writes, denied paths, denied network),\nbundle trailer/format validation, and build-time rejection of Node built-ins and CommonJS.\n\n## What is not enforced\n\n* No memory or CPU limit on script execution: an infinite loop freezes the window (QuickJS memory cap is\n  1 GiB, stack 2 MiB).\n* QuickJS and native crates are not hardened against malicious inputs; treat untrusted images, fonts and\n  HTML as a risk.\n* Scripts can read the whole bundle and their own `localStorage` (a plain JSON file in the user data\n  directory). Nothing is encrypted.\n* A bundle appended to an executable is not signed or integrity-checked by the runtime. Code signing is not\n  implemented.\n* `crypto.getRandomValues` uses the OS CSPRNG, but `crypto.subtle` does not exist.\n\n## Reporting\n\nOpen a private security advisory on the repository. Please include the bundle or script that reproduces\nthe behaviour.\n"
};
